<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caucasus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Caucasian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Caucasus is the mountainous region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>, lying between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. It was contested for centuries by successive powers, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>. In the nineteenth century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> conquered the region after long wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caucasus.jpg" alt="Caucasus" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bourrichon - fr:Bourrichon with English translations, additions, and corrections by Ketone16 (partly following Yuri K... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caucasus_topographic_map-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
